t. A schematic area illustration is not a prerequisite. The minimizer premise here belongs to the ordinary manuscript model; formal-interface hypotheses remain on the separate Lean target. This classification does not prove a transport between formal models.","citation_ids":["support_closure_source","support_closure_lean_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.no_bounded_gap","kind":"claim","label":"No bounded gap between support points","locator":"variation.tex:223–237; bounded-gap contradiction","source_id":"support_tex_variation","statement":"For an admissible minimizer gamma and its Stieltjes measure, no support-free interval (a,b) can have endpoints a,b in S with 0<=a<b<1. Constancy of gamma and contact give q(a)=a, q(b)=b and q'(a),q'(b)<=1. If the plateau height is positive, strict convexity gives q'(t) below the endpoint chord and below 1; if zero, strict increase gives q'(t)<q'(b)<=1. Integration contradicts q(b)-q(a)=b-a.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.no_bounded_gap","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.no_bounded_gap","id":"field:2c641dc14823882c9b882120e5bdbc45e90ed886ca4fca5683cf002ec0909050","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.no_bounded_gap","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.full_relative_support","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22support.full_relative_support%22%2